---
import { ancestryAudit, missingParents } from '../scripts/family/ancestry';
import { sharedById, ADAM, personUrl } from '../data/shared-family';
import { confirmedAncestryById as ancestryPeople, familyMapById, mapProfileUrl, mapEdgeAssessment } from '../data/family-map';
import { ancestryFindings } from '../data/ancestry-research';
const audit = ancestryAudit(ADAM, ancestryPeople);
const gapsByChild = audit.ids.filter(id => missingParents(ancestryPeople[id]).length).sort((a,b) => ancestryPeople[a].name.localeCompare(ancestryPeople[b].name));
---
<section class="ancestry-journey" id="ancestry-journey" aria-labelledby="ancestry-heading" data-ancestry-journey>
  <header><span class="editorial-kicker">The next chapter</span><h2 id="ancestry-heading">How far back can we go?</h2><p>Follow a single trail from Adam (Tom), see where names are missing, and check the records behind the oldest claims.</p></header>
  <div class="ancestry-stats"><p><strong>{audit.ancestors.length}</strong><span>supported ancestors</span></p><p><strong>{audit.longest.length-1}</strong><span>parent links on the longest trail</span></p><p><strong>{audit.gaps.length}</strong><span>unfilled parent positions</span></p></div>
  <p class="shared-provenance">These trails stop wherever a parent connection lacks explicit supporting evidence. A name in the imported tree alone does not extend a trail. Other supported family clusters are available through “All evidence-backed people” on the map.</p>
  <details class="ancestry-trails" open>
    <summary>Follow one ancestry trail</summary>
    <label class="ancestry-select">Trail endpoint <select data-ancestry-select>{audit.paths.map((path, i) => <option value={i}>{i===0?'Longest · ':''}{ancestryPeople[path.at(-1)!].name} · {path.length-1} parent links{i>0&&audit.paths.slice(0,i).some(p=>p.at(-1)===path.at(-1))?' · another route':''}</option>)}</select></label>
    <p class="ancestry-trail-help">Start at Tom and read downward into earlier generations. Open a name for its full profile, or “On the map” to explore that branch.</p>
    <div class="ancestry-trail-window" tabindex="0" aria-label="Ancestry trail; scroll to earlier generations">
      {audit.paths.map((path, i) => <div data-ancestry-path={i} hidden={i!==0}><ol class="ancestry-trail">{path.map((id, generation) => <li><span class="ancestry-generation">{generation===0?'You':`G${generation}`}</span><div><a href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{id===ADAM?'Adam Muncie (Tom)':ancestryPeople[id].name}</a><small>{ancestryPeople[id].dates || 'Dates not recorded'} · supported connection</small>{generation>0 && mapEdgeAssessment(id,path[generation-1],'parent').evidenceUrl && <a class="ancestry-review-link" href={mapEdgeAssessment(id,path[generation-1],'parent').evidenceUrl}>Supported parent connection · evidence ↗</a>}</div><a class="ancestry-map-link" href={`/family/?focus=${id}`}>On the map ↗</a></li>)}</ol>
        <div class="ancestry-unknown"><strong>Next generation: parents not yet supported</strong><ul>{missingParents(ancestryPeople[path.at(-1)!]).map(g => <li><a href={`#${g.id}`}>? · Unknown parent {g.slot}</a> <span class="family-confidence" data-confidence="provisional">placeholder</span></li>)}</ul><p>Earlier generations remain an open gap. Their number has not been established.</p></div>
      </div>)}
    </div>
    <p role="status" class="ancestry-trail-status" data-ancestry-status>Longest supported trail · {audit.longest.length-1} parent links · evidence-backed connections</p>
  </details>
  <details class="ancestry-gaps"><summary>Explore {audit.gaps.length} missing-parent placeholders</summary><p>Each placeholder has a permanent ID tied to an unfilled immediate parent position. Its identity, sex, dates, and biological or adoptive status are unknown. These are research positions, not additional identified relatives. More distant generations will be added only when their positions can be established.</p><ul class="ancestry-gap-list">{gapsByChild.map(id => <li><a href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{ancestryPeople[id].name}</a><div>{missingParents(ancestryPeople[id]).map(g => <details id={g.id}><summary>? · Unknown parent {g.slot} <span class="family-confidence" data-confidence={g.confidence}>provisional</span></summary><p>No supported parent connection established for this position. A possible name may still exist in the research archive.</p><small>Stable placeholder: {g.id}</small></details>)}</div></li>)}</ul></details>
  <details class="ancestry-research"><summary>Research archive · unresolved modern-family evidence</summary><p>These findings are retained for review, separately from the supported tree. They do not establish a continuous ancestry trail.</p>{ancestryFindings.filter(f=>f.people.some(id=>sharedById[id] || id.startsWith('p0'))).map(f => <article id={f.id}><h3>{f.title}</h3><span class="family-confidence" data-confidence={f.confidence}>{f.confidence}</span> <small>{f.sourceKind}</small><p>{f.finding}</p><p>{f.limit}</p><p><strong>Next record:</strong> {f.next}</p><p class="ancestry-citation"><a href={f.url}>{f.citation} ↗</a></p></article>)}</details>
  <noscript><p>Supported trails are listed above without scripting. Imported profile parent entries may still contain unverified claims. The missing-parent notes above also work without scripting.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>
  function initAncestry() {
    const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ancestry-journey]');
    if (!root || root.dataset.initialized) return;
    root.dataset.initialized = 'true';
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-ancestry-select]')!;
    select.addEventListener('change', () => {
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ancestry-path]').forEach(path => path.hidden = path.dataset.ancestryPath !== select.value);
      root.querySelector('.ancestry-trail-window')?.scrollTo({top:0});
      root.querySelector('[data-ancestry-status]')!.textContent = `${select.selectedOptions[0].textContent} · supported connections`;
    });
    const revealGap = () => {
      const target = document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));
      if (!target || target === root || !root.contains(target)) return;
      let parent: HTMLElement | null = target;
      while (parent && parent !== root) { if (parent instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) parent.open = true; parent = parent.parentElement; }
      target.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});
    };
    root.addEventListener('click', event => {
      const target = event.target instanceof Element ? event.target.closest<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[href^="#gap-"]') : null;
      if (target) { const gap = document.getElementById(target.hash.slice(1)); if (gap) { root.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('.ancestry-gaps')!.open = true; (gap as HTMLDetailsElement).open = true; } }
    });
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', revealGap);
    revealGap();
    document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap', () => window.removeEventListener('hashchange', revealGap), {once:true});
  }
  initAncestry(); document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initAncestry);
</script>
